## Residual risks (return)
| ID | Sev | Residual | Why not 7.1 FAIL |
|----|-----|----------|------------------|
| R1 | MED | Stmt `println` does not call `c_guard_scan_idents` (SPRINT **2.9**) | Token refuse + check dual still BLOCK; unify later |
| R2 | MED | LLVM builtin `print` is a println **shape** that skips check sink list **and** the walker; `emit-llvm` ALLOW | `print` not a typed product API; check type-fails; C emit is not `oo_print_*` |
| R3 | LOW | `print_err` / `log` / `fprintf` / `syslog` emit-secret / check-type-only (llvm no secret) | Same dual-path honesty as T2-4d; compile gate still rc≠0 on check |
| R4 | LOW | Unterminated `/*` or `//` in **malformed** C `args` would hide later idents | Product emit does not put comments in `args`; well-formed strings keep `/*`/`//` inside `"..."` |
| R5 | — | `${}` interp deep taint | SECRET_TAINT 5.8 — **not** 7.1 (string skip is correct) |
| R6 | — | 7.10 `c_parse_secret_env` `name = name + c` | Other OWN (memory/hygiene), not a sink FN |
| R7 | — | 7.2 `c_sys_exec_last_arg` | Sibling CRIT; not this close |
| R8 | — | Full IFC / `#[Secret]` / interproc beyond `__fr_secret__` | Named in SECRET_TAINT; do not greenwash |
| R9 | LOW | Check-result cache (`.ooda-cache/check`) can false-OK a refuse fixture (peer1) | Process residual; emit-c is the honest refuse rail |

**Explicitly not residuals of this close:** T1 return/alias/if-taint
(already FIXED); T2 field/args/comment-FP (already FIXED).

